From: Ameya Deshpande <fierbub.42069@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:43:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] imagination: Add native ASTC LDR texture support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The B-Series TPU decompresses ASTC natively (the stock driver reports
textureCompressionASTC_LDR = 1.0 for BXM-8-256), but this driver advertised the
feature as false and the format registry only listed ETC2/EAC formats, so
Switch and 3DS titles could not use their ASTC surfaces at all.

Register all 28 LDR formats (14 block sizes x UNORM/sRGB) against the texstate
compressed format indices 0-13 that the hardware already defines, add the
matching compressed border-colour entries using the U8U8U8U8 simple format (the
device has tpu_border_colour_enhanced), and drive
textureCompressionASTC_LDR from the device has_astc feature bit that every
B-Series profile already sets.

sRGB shares the UNORM hardware index because sRGB decoding is selected by the
image-word0 gamma bit, exactly as for the ETC2/EAC formats.

Verified: AArch64 driver links; the format/feature/border/texstate tables agree
across all 156 checks of the root repository's test_astc_format_coverage.py.
Not verified on silicon.

